// TEST: Unit Scale Integer Truncation (rejects)
// ERROR: BL3999
// An INTEGER value converts only by an exact integer factor. The
// unannotated sum joins at the LEFT operand (km), so the meter operand
// would scale by 1/1000 and truncate to zero. Rejecting beats silently
// returning zeros; the message names both escapes (a float element type, or
// an annotation putting the result in meter, where the factor is x1000 and
// exact). Note the asymmetry is real and intended: `b + a` below would be
// accepted, because converting meter -> km is what loses information, not
// km -> meter.
Unit meter
Unit km = 1000 * meter
let a: Int64<km> = 5
let b: Int64<meter> = 30
let c = a + b
